BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dreamcastmoe (USA) w/ Samatar and naga raani
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260510T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260510T220000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10001263-1778439600-1778450400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-21-at-11.01.27-am.png
CREATED:20260421T010435Z
DESCRIPTION:We couldn’t be more chuffed to be hosting Dreamcastmoe. The 
 Lost Tape series is worthy of a few spins and more. One not to be missed \
 n\n\n\nDreamcastmoe \n\n\n\nDreamcastmoe is a DJ\, producer\, and artist o
 ut of Washington\, D.C.\, making music that sits somewhere between R&B\, h
 ip hop\, soul\, and whatever else feels right in the moment. Since droppin
 g his Lost Tapes series\, he has been carving out a sound that feels perso
 nal\, loose\, and always evolving. \n\n\n\nHis music comes from real place
 s\, his city\, his experiences\, the people around him\, and that honesty 
 carries through everything he does. As things grow\, he stays focused on k
 eeping it genuine and making music people can actually feel\, not just hea
 r.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260421T010439Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/dreamcastmoe-usa-w-samatar-and-naga-
 raani/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Trivia
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260513T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260513T210000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10001784-1778697000-1778706000@ganggangcafe.com.au
CREATED:20260421T012136Z
DESCRIPTION:Trivia at Gang Gang. \n\n\n\nOn Wednesday night Quiz Meisters 
 come and host a trivia night for us. We’re talking pop culture\, politic
 s\, geography\, musical clues\, movie clues\, cryptic clues\, something fo
 r everyone!  Call us up to book a table inside if you’re keen to get qui
 zzy. A cancellation fee is charged if you do not show up to your booking 
 🙁 Otherwise you can enjoy regular service outside.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260421T012138Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/wednesday-trivia/2026-05-13/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cloud Ice 9 (MELB) w/ Olivia's World + edda | Gang Gang Cafe | pre
 s. by SONIC BUSINESS LTD
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260516T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260516T230000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10001259-1778958000-1778972400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-14-at-4.54.28-pm.png
CREATED:20260414T065747Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Cloud Ice 9 on their first East Coast Tour. Exorcisms of 
 apocalypse musings with a peppering of labyrinth woe. Plus Olivia’s Worl
 d and edda – down at Gang Gang Cafe. \n\n\n\nCloud Ice 9 emerge from
  the strange\, slow-burn creative fallout of Naarm’s long lockdowns. For
 med in the barns and attic sharehouses where hours of tinkering on toy key
 boards evolved into a fully-fledged “hive mind.” The result is one of 
 the most adventurous and bewildering sounds in the post-COVID Antipodes. D
 ifficult to pin down and even harder to predict\, Cloud Ice 9 twist famili
 ar genres into something uncanny. Fragments of post-punk\, experimental 
 pop\, and off-kilter grooves are warped by surreal storytelling\, robo
 t voices\, and an ever-expanding palette of oddball instrumentation. Acro
 ss releases like 8 Ball (2020)\, Circus St (2020)\, and Hocus Pocus 
 (2023)\, they’ve built a reputation for crafting immersive\, otherworldl
 y soundscapes. Their latest LP\, Globophobia (2025)\, is a darkly humor
 ous\, sci-fi-tinged odyssey through the absurdities of modern life. \n\n\n
 \nStep into the hive mind. Cloud Ice 9 are not to be missed. \n\n\n\nOlivi
 a’s World return to Canberra with their signature style of angular pos
 t-punk and dolewave-pop. In 2025 Olivia’s World debuted full-length a
 lbum Greedy & gorgeous\, the band’s third release following their two E
 Ps Olivia’s World (2019) and Tuff 2B Tender’(2021). In Greedy & go
 rgeous\, a quasi-concept album about desire\, Olivia’s World inhabitants
  deal with the woes of pleasure-seeking and a never-ending quest for beaut
 y. \n\n\n\nedda is a new Canberra band led by Joel Neville (Optic Nerve\,
  Lower Body\, Oxen\, Lapse). The band is a family – made up of spouse
 s\, siblings\, siblings-in-law\, childhood friends\, and ancient Icelandic
  origins.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T065748Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/cloud-ice-9-melb-w-olivias-world-edd
 a-gang-gang-cafe-pres-by-sonic-business-ltd/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sex Mask
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260524T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260524T220000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10002043-1779645600-1779660000@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-28-at-3.17.30-pm.png
CREATED:20260428T051752Z
DESCRIPTION:Freshly returned from a US tour and just announced for the Sle
 aford Mods national tour\, we are stoked to be hosting Sex Mask at GG \n\n
 \n\nVague pop instilled with the ancient genius of your own blood. \n\n\n\
 nSex Mask holds the many trigger words your CIA handler doesn’t want you
  to know.  \n\n\n\nWe have several testimonials from fans attesting to se
 mi-mystical experiences\,  \n\n\n\nsome claim it to be Deja vu from a gen
 etic memory long dormant and locked\, \n\n\n\nOthers speak of foreshadowed
  flashes of a past life they are yet to have lived. \n\n\n\nAll of this\, 
 incited after only seconds of exposure to any of our available songs. \n\n
 \n\nIs Sex Mask just another egregious attempt from delusional solipsists 
 at being heard while saying close to nothing? Yes. But we make it look goo
 d. \n\n\n\nPart Taoist riddle\, part lone gun-mans manifesto.  \n\n\n\nWe
  are also a post punk/alt rock band from Melbourne.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T051753Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/sex-mask/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Purelink (NYC) w/ Umki and Discobasis
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260531T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260531T220000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10002044-1780250400-1780264800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-28-at-3.20.07-pm.png
CREATED:20260428T052052Z
DESCRIPTION:urelink is an ambient music trio from Brooklyn\, New York City
 . The group\, comprised of Ben Paulson\, Tommy Paslaski\, and Akeem Asani\
 , formed in 2020 and has been described as an “ambient boyband.” Their
  debut release\, the single Bliss / Swivel\, was self-released in 2021\, 
 with both tracks later included on the 2023 EP To / Deep. More recently i
 n 2025 their album Faith was released\, featuring Loraine James and others
 . \n\n\n\nThe trio began collaborating after Ben Paulson\, known professio
 nally as Kindtree\, and Tommy Paslaski\, known professionally as Concave R
 eflection\, who had previously collaborated under the name All Light Hits 
 U\, met Akeem Asani\, who had been releasing under the name Millia\, in 20
 19. They began playing music together in early 2020\, using Ableton Live t
 o link their three computers over Wi-Fi\, which inspired the name Purelink
 . \n\n\n\nTo have them as part of their Australian tour is a real honour f
 or us\, we’ve been very big fans of Purelink since their first release. 
 To say the least we highly recommend coming\, sitting listening\, and gett
 ing to hear some very special music that is hard to come by. \n\n\n\nSuppo
 rts from amazing Umki and Discobasis.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T052054Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/purelink-nyc-w-umki-and-discobasis/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:anaiis
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260606T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260606T230000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10002045-1780772400-1780786800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-28-at-3.21.43-pm.png
CREATED:20260428T052323Z
DESCRIPTION:anaiis is coming to Aus and we are so happy we’re able to ho
 st her at Gang Gang. We’ve been listening to them a lot since booking th
 em\, a special artist making some incredible music \n\n\n\nanaiis \n\n\n\n
 As a teenager\, anaiis moved between France\, Ireland\, Dakar\, and the 
 United States\, relearning languages and searching for a sense of belongin
 g. With her music\, she’s channelled her yearning into a globe-spanning 
 sound grounded in open-hearted empowerment and Black feminism. \n\n\n\nPer
 forming her latest album\, Devotion and the Black Divine\, she embraces g
 race\, motherhood\, and the work of nurturing her inner child. With a voic
 e that moves from restrained falsetto to a deep\, rich alto\, she glides o
 ver reggae grooves\, warm synth chords\, and dark orchestral swells. Gospe
 l\, R&B\, and chamber pop bend with experimental flourishes and subtle voc
 al glitches.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T052325Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/anaiis/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hana Stretton
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260621T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260621T220000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10001258-1782064800-1782079200@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-14-at-9.43.02-am.png
CREATED:20260414T065308Z
DESCRIPTION:We are stoked to be working with Jet Black Cat again to presen
 t Hannah Stretton with Alice Barlow. \n\n\n\nHana Stretton is an accompli
 shed Australian-British multi-instrumentalist\, songwriter & producer. Bor
 n and raised on a farm in New South Wales\, Hana’s early life was steepe
 d in natural beauty and isolation\, which has become the influence for muc
 h of her music. Her work reflects a deep connection to her roots. \n\n\n\n
 Hana made her debut record\, Soon\, outside\, in still moments after fire
 s and wild storms had raged through her home in the Australian bush. Compl
 etely isolated with just her beloved cows and a few instruments\, recordin
 g music became a way to pass the hours. The album was self-released in Jan
 uary 2023\, with a vinyl run by boutique Australian label brierfield flood
  press. The following year\, P.W. Elverum & Sun (the private press of Phil
  Elvrum aka Mount Eerie) re-issued a special edition vinyl\, selling out a
 lmost instantly. Upon release\, Elvrum explained his admiration for Hana
 ’s music: “I hear an artist who has entered completely into the stream
  where creation originates […] Hana Stretton has truly recorded the deep
  flourishing sound of a quiet listening mind in full blossom.” \n\n\n\nA
 lice Barlow is a singer-songwriter\, composer and producer from South Eas
 t London known for her captivating live performances. Drawing on folk\, in
 die and alternative influences – her dark guitar tones\, haunting vocals
  and unique ear for melody have built a loyal following in London and beyo
 nd. With new singles on the way\, she is set to release her eagerly awaite
 d debut album on Domino Records this winter. This will be her first time i
 n Australia. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and sa
 fe experience for all. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with access
 ible restrooms. We have zero tolerance for harassment and have support mea
 sures in place to ensure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility n
 eeds or assistance\, please contact us in advance. We aim to make our even
 ts enjoyable for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnaw
 al and Ngambri people\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our e
 vents take place. We pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and
  emerging\, and recognise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\
 , and culture. We are grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal C
 ountry.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T065309Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/hana-stretton/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cut Worms (USA) with special guest John Andrews (USA)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260709T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260709T220000
DTSTAMP:20260507T184839
UID:ganggang-10001243-1783623600-1783634400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-17-at-11.30.21-am.png
CREATED:20260317T003144Z
DESCRIPTION:Transmitter is Max Clarke’s fourth full length record as C
 ut Worms\, due out March 13th via JagJaguwar. Produced by Jeff Tweedy at W
 ilco’s Loft studio\, Transmitter marks a deepening of Clarke’s abili
 ties and the convergence of two artists whose work searches for grace amid
  dislocation. Together\, they conjure the ecstatic spirits of power pop an
 d alt rock\, expanding Cut Worms’ vintage palette while reaffirming his 
 gift for timeless songwriting. \n\n\n\nWhile Clarke’s voice and writing 
 formed the framework\, Tweedy’s guitar and bass lines sketched the rooms
  the songs inhabit. Tweedy’s presence as a producer revealed itself not 
 in heavy-handed choices but in how he coloured spaces and continually offe
 red new textures. Between them\, their like-minded sensibilities bridged a
  generational gap to create something more nuanced than either might have 
 made alone. \n\n\n\nNow several albums into his career\, Clarke stands ful
 ly in command of his craft\, resonating at his own frequency. What began a
 s a passion for bygone pop has matured into a study of endurance itself\, 
 confirming him as a singer-songwriter of lasting depth. Transmitter finds 
 Clarke in full stride\, writing with the conviction of someone who’s mad
 e peace with uncertainty. These songs reckon with the cost of comfort and 
 return to the idea that beauty\, connection\, and love are not luxuries bu
 t necessities for survival. \n\n\n\nJohn Andrews has spent the past few ye
 ars tucked away in Red Hook\, Brooklyn – a neighborhood that sits just b
 eyond the natural drift of the city. Once shaped by maritime industry and 
 later a haven for artists in search of vast warehouse space\, its history 
 and isolation give it a quiet magnetism. Streetsweeper\, the fifth album
  by John Andrews & The Yawns\, reflects that vantage point-tranquil\, self
 -contained\, and curious about the movements most people overlook. \n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for al
 l. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We h
 ave zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to en
 sure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\,
  please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for eve
 ryone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri peopl
 e\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We
  pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and reco
 gnise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We ar
 e grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T065350Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/cut-worms-usa-with-special-guest-joh
 n-andrews-usa/
END:VEVENT
